            <ArticleTitle>[Treatment of pain in chronic calcifying pancreatitis with endoscopy and extracorporeal shock wave lithotripsy. A case report].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>505-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Abdominal pain is the most frequent symptom of chronic pancreatitis and may, on occasions, lead to great treatment problems. The case of a 56-years-old patient with idiopathic chronic pancreatitis calcifying who showed intracanalicular lithiasis is reported. Treatment with endoscopy and extracorporal shock wave lithotripsy (ESWL) was successful.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
